# R12: the séance at the spirit board in the parlor (H3). Speaker joseph_patrini (the butler's spirit, ALL CAPS, answers through the board). Region crooked_house.
# FINAL-WORDED: every line below is voiced as written; do not edit a line once the voice lane starts.
# Started by: the prop h3_spirit_board (`start`). Two or more hands on the planchette; the party chooses when (they may say "not yet" and explore first).
# The question menu grows as the house is explored (visited: floors) and as earlier answers are given, capped at eight questions; each answer is followed by the open
# roll (`roll`): a bite of cold on a failed roll steps up every time. Each bite is `damage <dice> psychic party` (every hand on the board; the engine never
# drops a hero below 1 Hit Point), counted by seance_stings: 1d4, 1d6, 1d8, 1d10, then 1d12 (stings 1..5, capped at 5). The roll is a Constitution check against the party's best (DC 6 stands in for the book's "1 on a d10").
# He answers "where is the attic door" with TROPHIES (sets trapdoor_known), "who is the cat" with LIAR, "what is Shuck" with SALLY.
# GOODBYE closes it for good: seance_done. When the three plot clues (the hag, the six mementos, the attic door) were all asked, he asks them to find his son.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_r12_seance/), edited.

~ start
if flag.seance_done
-> board_dead
endif
Narrator: A dusty spirit board sits on the round parlor table beside a cold, cobwebbed hearth, its wooden pointer marked A and D restin' between HELLO and GOODBYE. Reckon it is just waitin' on your hands.
-> hands_menu

~ hands_menu
* Lay our fingertips on the pointer and ask if anyone is here. -> begin
* [Arcana DC 10] Recall how a sitting like this is properly conducted. -> arcana_ok | arcana_miss
* Leave the board alone for now. -> END

~ arcana_ok
Narrator: You rest your fingertips light on the wood and ask one plain question at a time. Whatever listens in the dark spells its mind out letter by letter.
Narrator: Best mind your knuckles, though, for the dead can bite back with a climbing chill. Once that pointer touches GOODBYE, the board goes deaf and dumb for good.
-> hands_menu

~ arcana_miss
Narrator: You scratch around in your memory for parlor tricks and churchyard tales. All you come up with is a mouthful of dust and half a rumor.
-> hands_menu

~ begin
Narrator: Your fingertips settle on the wood, and the pointer gives a dry little shiver. Over in the cold hearth, a low flame catches with a crackle, and the whole room leans in close.
joseph_patrini: HELLO.
Narrator: The pointer stops dead on the last letter, patient as an old house servant awaitin' the bell. A thin, cellar cold settles into the pads of your fingers.
-> menu

~ menu
if flag.seance_asked_1 and flag.seance_asked_2 and flag.seance_asked_3 and flag.seance_asked_4 and flag.seance_asked_5 and flag.seance_asked_6 and flag.seance_asked_7 and flag.seance_asked_8
-> closing
endif
* [if not flag.seance_asked_1] Who are you? -> q1
* [if flag.seance_asked_1 and not flag.seance_asked_2] Who did this to you? -> q2
* [if not flag.seance_asked_3] Where are Phillip and Adela? -> q3
* [if flag.seance_asked_3 and not flag.seance_asked_4] Who is behind all of this? -> q4
* [if flag.seance_asked_4 and not flag.seance_asked_5] How do we get out of here, and what opens the way? -> q5
* [if flag.seance_asked_4 and not flag.seance_asked_6] Where is the door to the attic? -> q6
* [if visited:crooked_house_second and not flag.seance_asked_7] Who is the grey cat? -> q7
* [if visited:crooked_house_third and not flag.seance_asked_8] What is Shuck, the red dog? -> q8
* That is enough. Let us bid him goodbye. -> confirm_goodbye

~ q1
set seance_asked_1
Narrator: The pointer scrapes out from under your fingers, draggin' itself across the painted alphabet one slow letter at a time.
joseph_patrini: JOSEPH PATRINI. BUTLER.
joseph_patrini: I SERVED THIS HOUSE. I KEEP MY POST.
-> roll

~ q2
set seance_asked_2
Narrator: The pointer balks and catches on the grain, then jerks hard across the board like a mule pulled by the bit.
joseph_patrini: EUSTACE LOCKWOOD. MY MASTER.
joseph_patrini: HE SLEW US ALL.
-> roll

~ q3
set seance_asked_3
Narrator: The little wooden heart lifts a hair off the varnish and settles down square over YES.
joseph_patrini: ABOVE. ALIVE. NOT FOR LONG.
-> roll

~ q4
set seance_asked_4
Narrator: The pointer drifts in a slow, wide circle through the dust before it settles on a letter.
joseph_patrini: A HAG. IN THE ATTIC.
joseph_patrini: SHE WANTS THEIR SOULS FOR THE HOUSE.
-> roll

~ q5
set seance_asked_5
Narrator: The pointer swings sharp from corner to corner, quick and neat as a clerk tallyin' a ledger.
joseph_patrini: SIX KEEPSAKES OPEN THE WAY.
joseph_patrini: GEM. KEY. CUP. DOLL. BEAR. PIN.
joseph_patrini: THEY REST ON EVERY FLOOR. GATHER THEM ALL.
-> roll

~ q6
set seance_asked_6
set trapdoor_known
if quest.the_crooked_house == trapped or quest.the_crooked_house == mementos
quest the_crooked_house attic
endif
Narrator: The pointer creeps an inch, then darts straight across the varnish without a speck of hesitation.
joseph_patrini: TROPHIES.
joseph_patrini: LOOK UP.
-> roll

~ q7
set seance_asked_7
Narrator: The pointer shivers under your nails like a bare foot steppin' onto frosted iron.
joseph_patrini: LIAR.
joseph_patrini: HE HUNGERS FOR TALES. DO NOT FEED HIM.
-> roll

~ q8
set seance_asked_8
Narrator: The pointer slows right down and glides gentle across the painted arc, soft as a hand on a cradle.
joseph_patrini: SALLY.
joseph_patrini: SHE WAS A CHILD OF THIS HOUSE. SHE RUNS FREE NOW.
-> roll

# The open roll after every answer. A failed roll is a bite of cold; every bite is worse than the last.
~ roll
check Constitution DC 6 -> calm | sting

~ calm
Narrator: The pointer settles back still, and the draft stays down in the floorboards where it belongs. The board just waits on your next word.
-> menu

~ sting
set seance_stings += 1
if flag.seance_stings == 1
Narrator: The pointer bucks hard under your palms. A thin needle of winter cold runs straight through every hand on the wood.
damage 1d4 psychic party
endif
if flag.seance_stings == 2
Narrator: The board kicks back colder this time, sendin' a gray frost up past your wrists until your fingers go thick and numb.
damage 1d6 psychic party
endif
if flag.seance_stings == 3
Narrator: That third chill bites deep into the meat of your thumbs. It settles like hard pond ice inside the bones of every hand.
damage 1d8 psychic party
endif
if flag.seance_stings == 4
Narrator: The cold snaps up your arms and wrings the warm wind right out of your chests. Your stiff fingers scarce want to uncurl from the wood.
damage 1d10 psychic party
endif
if flag.seance_stings >= 5
Narrator: A black frost locks every arm to the elbow in a vice of winter iron. It holds you fast a long count before it lets go slow.
damage 1d12 psychic party
endif
-> menu

~ confirm_goodbye
Narrator: Reckon if you let the old fellow go now, this board ain't gonna speak twice. Whatever you leave unasked stays buried in the dark.
* Wait. Let us ask something else first. -> menu
* Let him go. -> closing

# His last words. The urgent clue is the first thing the party missed; with nothing missed, he warns of the hag's disguise and asks them to find his son.
~ closing
if not flag.seance_asked_4
-> urgent_hag
endif
if not flag.seance_asked_5
-> urgent_mementos
endif
if not flag.seance_asked_6 and not flag.trapdoor_known
-> urgent_door
endif
-> urgent_face

~ urgent_mementos
Narrator: Before you can lift your hands away, the pointer gives a sharp, hasty tug under your fingers.
joseph_patrini: SIX KEEPSAKES OPEN THE WAY. GEM. KEY. CUP. DOLL. BEAR. PIN.
joseph_patrini: SEARCH EVERY FLOOR. FIND THEM FIRST.
-> goodbye

~ urgent_hag
Narrator: Right before your fingers part from the wood, the pointer scrapes out one hasty warning.
joseph_patrini: A HAG WAITS IN THE ATTIC.
joseph_patrini: STOP HER WORK. MAKE HASTE.
-> goodbye

~ urgent_door
set trapdoor_known
Narrator: Just as you go to raise your hands, the pointer darts out with a sharp, urgent tap.
joseph_patrini: THE WAY UP IS HIDDEN. TROPHIES.
joseph_patrini: LOOK TO THE CEILING.
-> goodbye

~ urgent_face
Narrator: Before your fingers clear the varnish, the little wooden heart tugs back hard for one last word.
joseph_patrini: SHE WEARS THE LADY'S FACE.
joseph_patrini: DO NOT TRUST YOUR EYES. LOOK TWICE.
-> find_my_son

# Only reached when nothing was missed: all three plot clues (the hag, the six keepsakes, the attic door) were gathered.
~ find_my_son
set patrini_asked_find_son
quest find_my_son asked
Narrator: The pointer trembles in place a spell, like a man holdin' back a heavy word at the door.
joseph_patrini: ONE THING MORE. MY SON LIVES.
joseph_patrini: FRANCIS. PLEASE FIND HIM.
joseph_patrini: TELL HIM HIS NAME. PATRINI.
-> goodbye

~ goodbye
set seance_done
joseph_patrini: GOODBYE.
Narrator: The pointer slides down to the corner and stops dead. Over in the hearth, the fire hisses out like a doused lamp, takin' the chill with it.
-> END

~ board_dead
Narrator: Only dust sits on the painted letters now, cold and still under your hands. Some doors in this world only open the once.
-> END
